    "task_id": "wc-reduce-plan-core-to-validator",
    "goal": "Reduce runtime/plan_core.ts to the validator surface production actually reaches and remove the two orphans in runtime/v4_runtime.ts, using the compiler rather than a name list to decide which bodies are genuinely unreachable.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "PLC-1",
        "assertion": "runtime/plan_core.ts exports only the surface reached from production: PlanValidationError and projectPlanValidation, the two symbols runtime/v4_runtime.ts imports. The other 30 exports are de-exported first and only then deleted, and `bun run typecheck` is what determines which bodies are genuinely unreachable, because projectPlanValidation may retain internal call paths through symbols that look unused from outside. No symbol is deleted from a name list alone.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"run\",\n    \"typecheck\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 180000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 20000\n}\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "PLC-2",
        "assertion": "The two orphans in runtime/v4_runtime.ts are removed: the READ_ONLY_V3_COMMANDS constant, which is declared and referenced nowhere in the repository, and the unused `command` and `args` parameters of retiredResponse. The read-only v3 CLI wall itself is unchanged and still refuses the retired commands with the same message.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"test\",\n    \"tests/v4-runtime-launchers.test.ts\",\n    \"tests/v4-plan-control-plane.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 120000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 20000\n}\n"
      },
